<!-- STUDY PLAN -->
<section class="section" id="prep">
  <div class="section-title">Preparation Strategy & Study Plan</div>

  <div class="card">
    <div class="card-title"><div class="icon">📅</div> 6-Month Study Plan</div>
    <div class="month-card">
      <h4>Month 1–2 — Foundation</h4>
      <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--slate);">Build basics in all four subjects. Start with NCERT Mathematics (Class 6–10), basic Grammar (Wren & Martin), NCERT History/Polity/Geography, and easy reasoning puzzles. Target: complete the entire syllabus once at a surface level.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="month-card">
      <h4>Month 3–4 — Depth & Practice</h4>
      <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--slate);">Go deep on high-weightage topics. Solve chapter-wise questions from standard books (Rakesh Yadav for Maths, Kiran Publication for GK, R.S. Aggarwal for Reasoning). Read newspapers daily for current affairs. Target: 100+ questions solved per subject per week.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="month-card">
      <h4>Month 5 — Mock Tests</h4>
      <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--slate);">Take full-length mock tests under timed conditions — minimum 2 per week. Analyse every wrong answer. Focus on speed and accuracy. Identify weak areas and revisit them immediately after each test.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="month-card">
      <h4>Month 6 — Revision & PYQs</h4>
      <p style="font-size:13px; color:var(--slate);">Solve 10 years of PYQs. Maintain a formula sheet for Maths and a vocabulary notebook for English. Revise GK notes every 3 days. Target a score of 150+ in mock tests before the exam.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="tip-grid">
    <div class="tip-card">
      <div class="tip-num">01</div>
      <h4>Tier I is the Gateway</h4>
      <p>Most candidates fall at Tier I. Prioritise all 4 sections equally — no section should be below 60% accuracy.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="tip-card">
      <div class="tip-num">02</div>
      <h4>Time Management</h4>
      <p>Spend max 14 min/section in Tier I. In mock tests, practice moving on from difficult questions quickly.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="tip-card">
      <div class="tip-num">03</div>
      <h4>GK — Daily Habit</h4>
      <p>Read monthly GK digests. Cover science, awards, sports, and government schemes — SSC loves these.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="tip-card">
      <div class="tip-num">04</div>
      <h4>English — Vocabulary</h4>
      <p>Learn 10 new words daily. One-word substitutions and idioms are high-yield in Tier I and Tier II.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="tip-card">
      <div class="tip-num">05</div>
      <h4>Maths — Formula Sheet</h4>
      <p>Maintain a hand-written formula sheet. Geometry and trigonometry formulas are direct scoring opportunities.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="tip-card">
      <div class="tip-num">06</div>
      <h4>Don't Ignore Computers & Typing</h4>
      <p>Many top scorers fail because they ignore the Tier II Computer Knowledge or DEST typing test. Practice typing 15 mins daily.</p>
    </div>
